# PXQU tier map 'pxqu96-flashnext-6card-262k-ub2048': Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (arch qwen4exp),
# 48 layers, 512 experts, 10 used. COMPLETE map: one rule per quantizable tensor.
#
# TARGET  6 Tesla cards = 4x P100-PCIE-16GB + 2x V100-PCIE-16GB (95.088 GiB accounted),
#         -fa on, -c 262144 (native max), -b 2048 -ub 2048, -ctk f16 -ctv f16,
#         -sm layer, n_seq_max 1, per_layer_token_embd pinned to CPU.
# RESULT  on-card weights 72.167 GiB of 75.798 GiB cap; peak card 95.4%,
#         every card >= 0.5 GiB headroom. FITS.
# KV      9.11 GiB at 262144 f16 (12 full-attn layers + indexer + 36 delta-net states).
# FILE    122.83 GiB on disk, of which 50.664 GiB is host-side
#         (per_layer_token_embd, Q8_0, stays in RAM via -ot).
# EXPERTS 68.242 GiB, avg 4.8528 bpw, floor pxq4, hist {'pxq4': 59, 'pxq6': 85}.
#
# BUILT   2026-09-16, rc=0, 1224/1224 tensors, 5,059,459 ms (84.3 min) at 16 threads.
#   source $PXA_MODELS_DIR/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Uncensored-BF16-pleq8.gguf
#   out    $PXA_MODELS_DIR/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Uncensored-PXQU96-6card-262k.gguf
#   size   131304128928 B (122.28 GiB)
#   sha256 075c431c6270888d2bf45305a0d7c8aa3efae41e15a3d555c1a277322f5a5289
#   COMPOSITION MEASURED q8_0 42.0% + pxq6 35.7% + pxq4 21.2% + q6_K 0.8% + f32 0.2%
#   + f16 0.0%; PXQ-family 56.9%, 50% floor cleared unaided.
#   MAP SHA NOTE: this header was corrected after the build, so the working file's sha256
#   no longer equals the map that was consumed. The consumed map was
#   7e23e1e49a86e6726c8b530dd91a0c59fb1a5755fcadda1143a9d2c0d1c1e6a7 (rules-only
#   44738dac3ab24cfa03148bd943728e366b730a01270df6c409269e2cf6839bb6). Every RULE line
#   below is byte-identical to that build; only # comments changed.
#
# THIS IS AN EXTENSION OF THE HOUSE 4-CARD LADDER, NOT A NEW OBJECTIVE.
#   The 4-card recipe (pxqu-flashnext-4xp100-150k) spends 12 expert upgrades on a
#   REASONED ladder: ffn_down_exps before ffn_gate/up (this arch has NO ffn_norm and
#   NO output_norm -- build_qwen4exp.cpp:8-12, the hc mixer is the only normalisation --
#   so down's error enters the wide residual with nothing downstream to rescale it),
#   then by proximity to the sequence boundary (blk.0's MoE writes the residual every
#   later block reads; blk.47's is read by the head).
#   Sorting the house's own 144 rules by (rank, boundary distance) REPRODUCES its 12
#   pxq4 slots EXACTLY -- that is the check that this ladder is theirs and not invented.
#   Here the ladder is walked in its own order with a packing oracle: an upgrade is kept
#   only if the 6-card contiguous layer split still tiles. 85 of 144 slots are kept
#   (the 59 dropped are the ones whose layers sit on the tightest cards -- packing,
#   not priority, is what rejects them).
#   vs the 4-card recipe: floor pxq3(3.25) -> pxq4(4.25) bpw, avg 3.3458 -> 4.8528 bpw.
#
# SPLIT   gpu0(P100) L0-6 | gpu1(P100) L7-14 | gpu5(P100) L15-22 | gpu6(P100) L23-31 | gpu2(V100) L32-39 | gpu4(V100) L40-47
#         -ts 7,8,8,9,8,8
#
# RISK (unchanged from the house recipe, and it still stands): the down-before-gate/up
#   ordering is REASONED, not measured. No sens.json exists for qwen4exp and the shipped
#   GGUF carries no imatrix. An upgrade is exactly 100.00 MiB on gate/up AND on down, so
#   if a sensitivity sweep lands and re-ranks the families, the map re-solves inside the
#   same byte budget with no size change.
#
# BUILD (flags MUST precede the positionals; NO --imatrix -- PXQU ignores it and
#        consuming one measured WORSE 2026-08-24; never --override-kv expert_used_count):
#   PXA_PXQ_BACKBONE=v2,universal PXA_PXQ_COMPOSITION_OVERRIDE=1 \
#     llama-quantize --allow-requantize \
#       --pxq-universal pxqu96-flashnext-6card-262k-ub2048.tiers \
#       <first-shard-or-source>.gguf <out>.gguf PXQ_UNIVERSAL <threads>
#   PXA_PXQ_COMPOSITION_OVERRIDE=1 IS NOT NEEDED ON THIS MAP -- CORRECTED 2026-09-16,
#   AFTER BUILDING IT. The line here previously claimed the override was mandatory on
#   this arch because the PLE alone is ~41% of the file. That reasoning was carried over
#   from the 3-bpw four-card build, which measured 45.1% PXQ and did need it. THIS map
#   measures 56.9% PXQ-family (pxq6 35.7% + pxq4 21.2%) and the composition gate PASSED
#   UNAIDED -- no assertion line was printed. It is a higher-tier map, so PXQ bytes grow
#   while the PLE does not; the floor is cleared by the tiers, not by the override.
#   Carrying the env var is harmless and the build passed it. The CLAIM was the defect.
#   The four-card recipe says MANDATORY and is still correct FOR THAT MAP.
#
#   preflight.py BEFORE quantizing. It now models the QUANTISER'S OWN GATES, not the
#   pre-fix crash: a tensor with ne0 % 32 != 0 is copied through structurally before the
#   map is consulted (llama-quantize.cpp: quantize &= (tensor->ne[0] % 32 == 0)), and so
#   are norms / ffn_gate_inp / ffn_gate_tid2eid / per_layer_token_embd / ssm_conv1d /
#   ssm_x / ssm_dt / attn_rel_b. ne0=4 tensors (ple_conv1d, ssm_conv1d) therefore get NO
#   RULE: naming a block-32 codec there would be inert at best and a crash before the fix.
#   On THIS map the instrument reports 390 copied by gates, 834 reached the map,
#   unmatched 0, PREFLIGHT OK. The previous note here described the old tool's failure;
#   see preflight-regression-pxqu96.md -- a stale check must not block a good map, and a
#   map must never be deformed to satisfy a tool.
#
# SERVE
#   llama-server -m <model>.gguf -ngl 99 -sm layer \
#     -ot 'per_layer_token_embd\.weight=CPU' -c 262144 -b 2048 -ub 2048 \
#     -ts 7,8,8,9,8,8 --jinja
#   -sm graph is REFUSED on a PXQ file at load (a PXQ row keeps one fp16 anchor per row
#   in its 64-row panel header, which covers all of K; graph mode splits along K).
#
# Consumed by llama-quantize --pxq-universal. Format: <ECMAScript regex>=<ggml type>
